al situation we did a quick  math calculation to figure out how much  I needed for a salary so I could try  think  [ __ ] what would work I got what I  thought we needed and it's like a month  or two into me at the new job and I was  wrong on the math we were struggling we  had had our first son here before and we  had the birthday party I had gone to the  store to buy you know food to feed our  family and you know as I'm driving there  I'm thinking to myself okay so this card  is has like ten dollars left on it this  card has like $20 left on it I'm like  there's no way I'm gonna be able to pay  for all this food we had the birthday  party but I was I was just done I was so  tired of playing the game and shortly  after that I listened to Dave's book  because a friend had recommended it to  us and it was one of those we're like  sure why not let's try it you know kind  of thing because we had no other option  at that point and so I listened to it in  a day and I was like Justin you have to  listen to this if you do nothing else to  this week today whatever listen to this  book because that's we need to do this I  don't care what you think about it where  I was doing it she asked me to read the  book and I told her no for a few weeks  and then just one day I downloaded it  and put it on audio on my car finish the  book in a matter of just a few hours  came home and said alright honey let's  cut up the credit cards something  clicked it was like it was that turning  point that made me realize that we have  to do something different and it was  that information that helped just kind  of structure it in a way that made sense  that nobody else had laid it out like  that well we had a plan then once we had  like something to follow or some sort of  you know guidelines it made all the  difference in the world but you know it  was it was definitely a turning point in  not only our financial situation but our  relationship as well I'm not saying just  because we read the book it changed  everything but it gave us the path to  start changing  I'd say probably bout six weeks after we  read the book we  Financial Peace University age we were  already into the budget we already had  started paying some stuff off before we  did it you don't even really realize how  bad the situation is until you put it on  paper wait what the heck did we do here  and you kind of have a real aha moment  when you actually sit down and go  through it which i think was part of  where that was is you really add it up  it's like we really do need to do  something here or we're not putting our  kids through college we're not moving  forward in life and then it hit me  about a few months in that a huge chunk  of our budget was the car payment the  truck that I so rightfully deserved but  I realized that that car payment could  open up a huge door in our budget so I  came home and I said to where we need to  sell the truck and she couldn't believe  that I had even brought that it was one  of those like who are you and what have  you done with my husband  that truck was part of I deserved it but  it also gave me the opportunity to try  to show off to people and I realized  that that's not what life's about  and that's not why we do what we do on a  daily basis and just giving that up was  not only a huge benefit the budget but  it was it whole emotional change in our  relationship and allowed us to just kind  of look at things differently  the biggest I think driver of that whole  problem was that I was a very selfish  person I was okay it was all about me  and I love to entertain but I love to  entertain to show off not to entertain  to make other people happy as much as  that's not necessarily a financial thing  makes you realize what our role is in  the whole process in it I think that  opened up my eyes to where I looked at  life in general I think that was a big I  just changed yeah the book the Total  Money Makeover was a complete  perspective change I think for both of  us don't be normal like Dave says all  the time be weird it's it's awesome to  not have the burden of you know society  I guess you could say on you and you  know just living with a purpose and  having your money work for you instead  of you just working for your money and  knowing where your money's going it  definitely is a huge life changer  everybody that we knew thought we were  crazy and after we did that free scream  her co-workers all saw it my co-workers  saw it a lot of our friends had seen it  and many of them now are doing it but  here you genuinely do it for the right  reasons and you don't care what the  world around you things you're doing it  because this is what God wants you to do  that's just cool how what that ends up  spider webbing into that's what this  whole thing is is you just build  momentum and just allow that to continue  to progress in it it's amazing what  continues to happen in a positive  direction in life it's just it was a lot  to go through and to take 17 months and  pay off 85,000 it was a struggle but at  the end looking back it was worth every  bit of sacrifice  to it I would not change I would not  change it for the world  change a 3-2  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

